<p><img src="https://cdn3.brettterpstra.com/uploads/2026/08/graffitimac-header-rb.7535.jpg" width="800" height="226" style="margin:0 auto;clear:both;" class="header" /></p>

<p><a href="https://graffiti.moe">Graffiti Moe</a> started as a terminal thing on purpose. <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">curl</code> a random spray, slap one up with a one-liner, feel like you’re tagging a wall that only nerds walk past. Fun. Also&hellip; a little exclusive.</p>

<p>I wanted that same fun for people who never open Terminal. So I built <strong>GraffitiMac</strong> — a tiny menu-bar app that lives next to your clock and occasionally reminds you that the wall is still weird and alive.</p>

<h3 id="login-spray-on-demand-spray">Login spray, on demand spray</h3>

<p><img src="https://cdn3.brettterpstra.com/uploads/2026/08/menubar.jpg"></p>

<p>Turn on <strong>Open at Login</strong> and every time your Mac wakes up into the day, you get a random spray in a little HUD. No Dock icon. No fuss. Just a piece of anonymous ASCII (or plain text) floating in for a few seconds.</p>

<p>Not in the mood to reboot for fun? Hit <strong>Show spray</strong> from the menu bar whenever you want another one. Same wall, same chaos, your schedule.</p>

<h3 id="spray-without-leaving-the-desktop">Spray without leaving the desktop</h3>

<p>Prefer to contribute instead of lurk? <strong>Spray…</strong> opens the graffiti.moe compose page right from the menu bar. Paint a tag, send it, go back to whatever you were pretending to work on.</p>

<h3 id="flag-the-junk">Flag the junk</h3>

<p>The wall is anonymous and mostly unfiltered, which is the point — and also why a <strong>Flag</strong> button exists on the HUD. See something that doesn’t belong (hate, spam, pure noise)? Flag it. Those get reviewed. You’re not the hall monitor; you’re just helping keep the wall worth reading.</p>

<h3 id="come-spray-something">Come spray something</h3>

<p>If you’ve been watching from the sidelines, this is your nudge. The Mac app is free. The site is free. The whole thing is open source:</p>

<p><a href="https://github.com/ttscoff/graffitimoe">https://github.com/ttscoff/graffitimoe</a></p>

<p>Grab GraffitiMac from <a href="https://graffiti.moe">the site</a> (Mac App → Download) or from GitHub Releases, leave it in the menu bar, and add your own mark to the wall. The terminal crowd will still be curling. You can just click.</p>

<p>By the way, you can find a lot of fun ASCII (plain text) art at
<a href="https://www.asciiart.eu/gallery">asciiart.eu</a>. And you can draw with
<a href="https://monodraw.helftone.com/">Monodraw</a> or online
with <a href="https://www.asciiart.eu/ascii-draw-studio">the ascii draw studio</a>,
to keep things interesting.</p>

